<%- include('partials/top', { description: 'How EasyNotes handles copyright, and how rights holders can ask for notes to be taken down.' }) %>
<div class="wrap narrow doc">
  <h1>Copyright and takedown</h1>
  <p class="muted">EasyNotes is a marketplace for notes that students and graduates write themselves. We respect the rights of institutions, lecturers, authors and publishers, and we act quickly when someone tells us their material is being sold here without permission.</p>

  <h2>What sellers may and may not sell</h2>
  <p>Sellers may sell their own summaries, explanations and worked examples. They may <strong>not</strong> sell, in full, in part, or as photos or screenshots:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>lecture slides, lecturer notes or handouts</li>
    <li>pages or passages copied from textbooks, study guides or course packs</li>
    <li>past exam papers, class tests or their memos</li>
    <li>assignment, tutorial or test answers given out by an institution</li>
    <li>anything downloaded from an institution’s learning platform</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Every seller’s identity and degree are verified, every seller confirms each upload is their own work under our <a href="/seller-terms">seller terms</a>, and uploads are automatically checked for signs of copied material.</p>

  <h2>How to ask for notes to be taken down</h2>
  <p>If you own the copyright in material that appears in notes on EasyNotes (or you’re authorised to act for the owner):</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Open the notes on EasyNotes and choose <strong>Report these notes</strong>, then <strong>I own the copyright (takedown request)</strong>. Or email <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>?subject=Takedown%20request"><%= supportEmail %></a>.</li>
    <li>Tell us which notes (the link), which of your material appears in them and where, and how you own it.</li>
    <li>Include your full name and contact details, and confirm that the information is accurate and that you believe in good faith the use isn’t authorised.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>What happens next</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We acknowledge your request by email.</li>
    <li>Within <strong>2 working days</strong> we review it and, if it’s well founded, remove the notes from sale. We may remove them straight away while we look into it.</li>
    <li>We tell the seller and give them the chance to respond. If they show the material is theirs or used lawfully, we may restore the notes and tell you.</li>
    <li>Sellers who repeatedly infringe have their accounts closed.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Students who already bought removed notes</h2>
  <p>When notes are removed for copyright reasons they’re taken off sale immediately. We may also refund buyers and recover the amount from the seller.</p>

  <h2>Misuse</h2>
  <p>Please only send a takedown request for material you own or are authorised to act for. False or misleading requests may be ignored.</p>
</div>
<%- include('partials/bottom') %>
